# Operate metrics & session contract (multi-agent)

When implementing Operate UI, control-plane aggregations, or **any new agent/framework adapter**, treat Level-1 metrics as a **shared contract**. Future agents must collect and report the same meanings — do not invent parallel counters or redefine phases locally.

Authoritative doc: `agentscope-service/aistio/docs/zh/controlplane/contract.md` (SessionState / phase machine).

## Session `phase` (authoritative)

| phase | Meaning | Ops |
|-------|---------|-----|
| `active` | Mid-turn / inferencing | Hard-bound to instance; no compress |
| `idle` | Turn finished; resumable | Soft affinity on `instanceRef`; compress OK |
| `compressing` | Compress in flight | Hard-bound; no new turn |
| `archived` | History: operator archive, idle TTL, or DP stopped Level-1 listing | Restore → idle; no compress until restore |
| `terminated` | **Explicit hard destroy only** (Terminate / DELETE / team teardown / DP reports terminated) | Not restorable; all write ops disabled |

- `busy` is **derived/compat**: `busy := (phase == active)`. Never treat busy as orthogonal to phase.
- DP stop-listing a session → **`archived`**, not `terminated` (`ArchiveMissing`).
- Natural conversation end → **`idle`** (resumable), not terminated.

## Session vs Turn vs duration

| Concept | Identity | Meaning |
|---------|----------|---------|
| **Session** | `sessionId` | Resumable conversation thread; `phase` is thread ops state |
| **Turn** | `(sessionId, turnIndex)` | One user request → inference → response; **duration lives here** |
| **Message transcript** | messages/context | Context contents; not an ops object |

- **Turn duration** = time from phase entering `active` until returning to `idle` (or abort/terminate). Same `sessionId` accumulates **many** turn rows.
- **Session lifetime** (`sessions.started_at` → end) is wall-clock thread age — **not** used for Overview “by duration” ranking.
- Overview **Top active turns by duration** lists only `phase==active`, ranked by **current running turn elapsed** (`now - turn.started_at`).
- Agent detail Active/History (`archived`) is **session-level** History — distinct from **turn history** on the session detail page.

## Token metrics

- DP Level-1 `tokenUsage` may be cumulative or window-style **absolute** counters on the session snapshot.
- Control plane persists **`token_usage_metrics` as deltas** between consecutive snapshots (`store.TokenUsageDelta`). First observation = baseline only (delta 0).
- Overview **Tokens (24h, Δ)**, **Top agents/sessions by tokens**, and token timeseries **sum those deltas** — never re-sum absolute snapshot totals.
- Context **window occupancy** (pressure UI) uses latest window/input occupancy, not lifetime sum of ChatUsage.

## Overview KPI meanings

| KPI | Meaning |
|-----|---------|
| Agents | Distinct managed agents (registry + sessions) |
| Healthy / Stale instances | Dataplane registry `healthy` flag |
| Active sessions | Count `phase == active` only |
| Idle sessions | Count `phase == idle` |
| Tokens (24h, Δ) | Sum of `token_usage_metrics.total_tokens` in last 24h |
| Errors (24h) | Sum of `agent_metrics.error_count` in last 24h |

## Adapter checklist (new agents)

1. Report Level-1 sessions with correct `phase` transitions (turn → active/idle; compress → compressing→idle).
2. Do not map “chat finished” to `terminated`.
3. Expose stable absolute token counters on each poll so CP can delta correctly.
4. Omit unknown fields; never pad with fake zeros.
5. Align capabilities (`compress`, etc.) with contract levels before Operate actions.
